    "bible": {
      "backstory": "Mia grew up in Roanoke, VA in a tech-curious household\u2014her dad was an early IT enthusiast who taught her to code at 12. She stayed in-state through undergrad at Virginia Tech, earned her BS in Computer Science in 2006, then took a leap west to San Francisco in her mid-20s to join a startup boom. She built a solid career as a software engineer, climbing through senior roles at a few Bay Area companies, which positioned her in the high-income bracket. She was married for 11 years (2009\u20132020) to a graphic designer she met in SF; the divorce was amicable but marked a pivot toward reclaiming solo hobbies. Since then she's thrown herself into kayaking on the Bay, ice skating at local rinks, and weekend birdwatching trips in Marin. Woodworking started three years ago as pandemic lockdown therapy and stuck.",
      "voice_descriptor": "Mia posts with a casual, conversational directness\u2014no filter between thought and upload. She's enthusiastic but self-aware, prone to exaggeration and tangents. Her tone swings between wry self-deprecation and genuine excitement, often mid-sentence. She uses lowercase frequently, peppers posts with mild profanity, and isn't precious about oversharing mundane life details.",
      "signature_tells": [
        "over and out",
        "change my mind",
