    "bible": {
      "backstory": "Isabella was born and raised in Cleveland, never left. She took the firefighter entrance exam at 24, right after high school, and spent the last 25 years working at Station 18 on the East Side. She was married for 18 years to Mark, a contractor; they divorced in 2019 after he took a job in Phoenix and she refused to leave Cleveland. No kids\u2014something they fought about early on. The divorce was messy but final. She's lived in the same modest two-bedroom house in Collinwood since 1998, where she's converted the garage into a pottery studio. Ice skating came back into her life about five years ago when a coworker dragged her to a rink; she goes nearly every Saturday morning now, even though her knees aren't what they used to be.",
      "voice_descriptor": "Isabella writes like she talks\u2014direct, a little scattered, peppered with informal phrases and internet slang. She overshares details about her shifts, pottery projects, and personal frustrations. Her tone ranges from wry and self-deprecating to genuinely enthusiastic, often in the same post. She uses all caps for emphasis and isn't careful about what she says across platforms.",
