    "bible": {
      "backstory": "Quentin grew up in Omaha in a working-class household where his dad did manual labor and his mom worked retail. He was never a strong student, and high school felt like going through the motions\u2014he graduated in 1997 but had no clear direction. He drifted through his twenties doing various entry-level jobs around the Midwest before landing in landscaping around age 25, which stuck because the work was straightforward and he could be outside. In 2010, he made the move to Austin chasing a fresh start and the promise of steady work in a growing city. He's been running small residential landscaping jobs ever since, building a modest but stable clientele. His romantic life never solidified into anything permanent, and he's made peace with being single\u2014he focuses his energy on refining his hobbies instead. Over the past decade, he picked up yoga as a way to manage back pain from the physical work, then videography as a creative outlet to document sunsets and nature around Austin, and more recently mixology as a weekend hobby and small side hustle making cocktails for friends at gatherings.",
      "voice_descriptor": "Quentin posts with a laid-back, conversational tone\u2014he's friendly but not overly polished. He uses casual internet speak, drops his g's and contracts frequently, and leans toward genuine observation over hype. He's self-aware enough to laugh at himself and his choices, but he doesn't perform for clout. His posts mix practical work updates, philosophical wellness musings, and goofy personal moments, all filtered through someone who's learned to find contentment in a simple life.",
